title: 'xcm: taking a zero amount from holding takes nothing'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Taking a zero amount from `AssetsInHolding` now returns nothing instead of a 0 entry, and a zero
    amount always counts as contained, so `ExpectAsset` with a zero amount succeeds.

    This fixes `FixedRateOfFungible::refund_weight` for refunds worth less than one unit: it
    panicked in debug builds and put a 0 entry into holding in release builds. `UsingComponents`
    and `TakeFirstAssetTrader` return the payment untouched on a 0 fee.
crates:
- name: staging-xcm-executor
  bump: patch
- name: staging-xcm-builder
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-primitives-utility
  bump: patch
